From ab6304061db3282be45bd3466de956df0ac793a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FileZilla dark mode port <fzdark@localhost>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:42:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] build: ignore additional in-tree MSYS2 build output

Upstream's rules assume 'make install' plus an NSIS build. Building in the
source directory on MSYS2 also leaves libtool wrappers, the version.rc and
MacInfo.plist substitutions, precompiled headers, .dirstamp stamps and the
data/dlls_gui NSIS staging behind. The gettext .mo output lands next to the
.po sources too, which the upstream 'locales/*/LC_MESSAGES/*.mo' rule does
not cover.

Without these, git status is unreadable and 'git add -A' sweeps binaries into
the patch series. Note Makefile.in stays ignored on purpose: nothing generated
is versioned here, because the build script reruns autoreconf and
reconfigures from configure.ac on every build.

The rules are added at the top of the file rather than appended. Upstream
ends .gitignore with a CRLF-terminated "*.log" line, and git am pipes the
patch through git mailinfo, which strips that CR, so any hunk using that line
as context can never match. Appending there produced a series that applied
with git apply but failed under git am.
---
 .gitignore | 41 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 41 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 747a193..4108e87 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -1,3 +1,44 @@
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Additions for building in-tree on MSYS2/UCRT64.
+#
+# The upstream rules further down assume `make install`/`make dist` and an NSIS
+# build. Building an unpatched GUI tree in the source directory produces a good
+# deal more, and without these rules `git status` cannot be read and `git add -A`
+# would sweep binaries into the patch series.
+#
+# This block sits above the upstream rules on purpose. Upstream ends .gitignore
+# with a CRLF-terminated "*.log" line, and `git am` runs the patch through
+# `git mailinfo`, which normalises that CR away. Any hunk whose context included
+# that line would therefore be unmatchable, so the additions are kept clear of it.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+# libtool wrappers and configure substitutions that are not .in templates
+libtool
+/src/fzshellext/version.rc
+/src/interface/resources/version.rc
+/src/interface/resources/MacInfo.plist
+
+# precompiled headers and automake directory stamps
+*.gch
+*.pch
+.dirstamp
+
+# NSIS staging from data/dllcopy.sh, which only runs under MAKENSISSCRIPT
+/data/dlls_*/
+/data/dll_*_install.nsh
+/data/dll_*_uninstall.nsh
+/data/*langfiles.nsh
+/data/libtoolexecutablesubdir.nsh
+/data/test_libtool_exedir.*
+
+# the Windows shell extension builds, which we do not produce
+/src/fzshellext/32/
+/src/fzshellext/64/
+
+# gettext merges the .po files in place, so the output lands next to the source
+locales/*.mo
+locales/*.po.new
+
 # autotools / automake build output
 Makefile
 Makefile.in
-- 
